 [17592186106009 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106009 #edb/ref 1050 540.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106009 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2fb56d40-545a-510d-a693-25bf992fdb77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106553 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106553 #edb/ref 1061 119188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106553 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f6dcb244-ba60-524d-bafc-0fd7ed3097aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106553 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106554 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106554 #edb/ref 1061 119189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106554 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91bb4d37-5646-5ecb-b152-184d3a1e7df5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106554 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106555 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106555 #edb/ref 1061 119192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106555 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "542a4e61-51eb-5729-8e5c-2bd1bfdc8f6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106555 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106556 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106556 #edb/ref 1061 119193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106556 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b1672354-ac07-5ce6-aea9-42ade75a5756" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106556 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106557 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106557 #edb/ref 1061 119196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106557 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5963d13b-c8a9-5e42-9832-539b63c97ffd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106557 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106558 #edb/ref 1061 119199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106558 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6be9e91b-24ac-5965-9577-4a57a3357b17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106558 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106559 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106559 #edb/ref 1061 119202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106559 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "60bdea8a-315f-547f-a828-49aa84b406ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106559 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106737 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106737 #edb/ref 1061 623181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106737 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2dd79ef0-aa4a-5d52-ba67-92d8d47fd909" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106737 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106738 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106738 #edb/ref 1061 623182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106738 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "48b5c886-bff4-52b2-b702-6be7c990ade1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106738 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106739 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106739 #edb/ref 1061 623185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106739 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2154c4c2-efe1-5888-87e0-905e612555d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106739 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106740 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106740 #edb/ref 1061 623186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106740 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2896eab9-aca7-5163-8e08-2101c4fa2827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106740 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106741 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106741 #edb/ref 1061 623189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106741 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ffc5ce2a-4bcb-5660-a1ce-e79bd1b4c604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106741 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106742 #edb/ref 1061 623190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106742 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ec3bbafa-69db-5676-8013-221157e979a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106742 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107044 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the triangle $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](images/46/46a85010d46969ffb7df440efd72bb3fa8d1394b35cc2887ee4567cda15079c5.png)\n\nThe sum of the length of its sides is called the **perimeter**. Here, the perimeter of our triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\  & =2+4.2+3.8 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107044 #edb/ref 1065 2244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107044 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7664d7c3-e47c-57b6-97aa-1131f036852c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107044 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107045 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we have a quadrilateral $ABCD$ as shown below and it is known that ${AD} = 6\\,\\mathrm{m},$ ${AB} = 2\\,\\mathrm{m},$ ${BC} = 4\\,\\mathrm{m},$ and $CD=5\\,\\mathrm{m}.$ What is the perimeter of the quadrilateral?   \n\n![](images/a7/a74251f1c72eccad42b98e0d3fd9a7e7cd0a60018a6f03bb65ec2abc34eb1c88.png)\n\nRemember that the **perimeter** $p$ of a polygon is the sum of the measures of all its sides. So, we can simply calculate \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AD+AB+BC+CD \\\\  & =6+2+4+5 \\\\  & =17\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107045 #edb/ref 1065 2246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107045 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0428807f-e6a6-5280-81bc-ab454203aebf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107045 #edb/ref 1067 "Perimeters of Polygons" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107046 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's take a look at the polygons depicted below and find their perimeters.\n\n![](images/69/69ef06a71f13625ad4525a03966f4a4c62ae2b2136b085e97b8dc02a6a6963cc.png)\n\nFrom the picture, we conclude that polygons I, II and III all have a perimeter of $10$ while polygon IV has a perimeter of $8.$ \n\nPolygons that have the same perimeter are called **isoperimetric**. So I, II and III are isoperimetric polygons." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107046 #edb/ref 1065 2247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107046 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "596db00e-9cf7-51e1-902e-73c6670780eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107046 #edb/ref 1067 "Isoperimetric Polygons" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107160 #edb/ref 1064 "![](images/24/24c4c952103f245cd4dc32e34d5dd2363478f5400ddecfbe2503130135c01946.png)\n\nConsider the regular pentagon above. What is the measure of each interior angle?\n\nRecall that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides equals $180^\\circ \\cdot (n-2).$ \n\nAll interior angles in a regular polygon are congruent. So, to calculate the measure of each interior angle, we find the sum of the interior angles and divide by the number of angles.\n\nA pentagon has $n=5$ sides. Therefore, the sum of its interior angles is\n\n$$\n180^\\circ \\times (5 - 2) = 540^\\circ.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the measure of each interior angle is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{540^\\circ}{5} = 108^\\circ,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/a7/a74a23a8dd760a31a0888eb694e36978c4767fd32bca6fae4fe8fe380c85e2e1.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107160 #edb/ref 1065 7912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107160 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d7abf1fc-4082-5a4f-a8ea-a74559737f2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107160 #edb/ref 1067 "Interior Angles of Regular Polygons" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107161 #edb/ref 1064 "A **regular polygon** is a polygon where all sides are congruent (have the same length), and all interior angles are congruent (have the same measure).\n\nSome examples of regular polygons are shown below.\n\n![](images/d3/d33f23d3d3e301e336d7f70f37e88eee0f605c31b098969805d7c6346e34470e.png)\n\nSome examples of polygons that are **NOT** regular are as follows:\n\n- The rectangle below is **NOT** regular since the sides are not all congruent.\n\n![](images/6d/6d0c6eaee1ae1932d3bd44013c0b8aca977cbe0d98242d5c10aaa24d4f281a77.png)\n\n- The rhombus below is **NOT** regular since the interior angles are not all congruent.\n\n![](images/ce/ce2b908945db56934f08dc0da47f6c708f5220bce3a80f5147362c8b915c5613.png)\n\n- A $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle is **NOT** regular since neither the sides nor the angles are all congruent.\n\n![](images/bf/bfe00eb1d1374252fd12f6c74eff7c052021a7305ce10027efc8869f561e3ef5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107161 #edb/ref 1065 7926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107161 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "cd59495c-0fc7-5db8-8d91-05d02fa8e26f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107161 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107165 #edb/ref 1064 "![](images/8e/8e128a2320d2658cc61cf83a1871d09caa7e4527b684c2af9086f80a00ecc717.png)\n\nConsider the regular hexagon above. What is the measure of each *exterior* angle?\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The exterior angles in a regular polygon are all congruent.\n\n- The sum of the exterior angles of *any* convex polygon equals $360^\\circ.$\n\nSo, to find the measure of the exterior angles of a regular polygon, we divide $360^\\circ$ by the number of sides.\n\nSince a regular hexagon has $n=6$ sides, the measure of each exterior angle is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{360^\\circ}{6} = 60^\\circ,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4f4538d9e2e09715fa3aa2035cd8b22cdc326b0ac02326551d193f26f1946473.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107165 #edb/ref 1065 9042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107165 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "754fe990-2a6b-5799-bb6d-bd83d8b8fff4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107165 #edb/ref 1067 "Exterior Angles of Regular Polygons" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110780 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110780 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Value of a Variable That Makes a Rectangle a Square" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110780 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110780 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "71118d0d-bd31-5af1-a881-608b88f777d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110781 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110781 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110781 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110781 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Measures of the Sides of a Rectangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110781 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110781 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6ff69d0d-cc28-5528-be82-d874fbecb064" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110782 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110782 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110782 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110782 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Measure of a Diagonal of a Square" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110782 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110782 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c9f0fffa-aef8-5f2e-af1b-32d67dd954a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110783 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110783 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110783 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110783 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110783 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Value of a Variable That Makes a Given Quadrilateral a Rectangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110783 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110783 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0730375d-ba61-5f0a-85f3-23c9535f7a38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186499475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186499493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Congruent Polygons on a Grid" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110790 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2e2f2884-829b-5e09-8fc0-16556b177732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110791 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110791 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110791 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186499487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110791 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Congruent Polygons Given Side and Angle Measures" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110791 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110791 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "30fc8daf-a6eb-537b-b19b-06ad5504b5e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186499465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186499533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186499557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing a Congruence Statement" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110792 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "46dbecc9-70e8-55c9-b7d7-7b5629ea1549" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
